---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import siteData from "../../content/site.json";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Sage and learn about the taste behind Good Intentions.">
  <section class="page-hero page-hero-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Picked and styled by Sage</span>
    <h1>Good Intentions changes with the mood.</h1>
    <p>One collection might be glossy 2000s pop. The next could be lace, velvet, festival color, or something a little witchy. Sage is the part that ties it together.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section founder-story-grid">
    <div class="founder-portrait-placeholder" aria-label="Founder portrait placeholder">
      <span>Photo of Sage<br />coming here</span>
      <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </div>
    <div class="founder-story-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">The person behind the rack</span>
      <h2>The common thread is Sage.</h2>
      <p>Her collections often begin with a song, a movie, a mood, or one piece that is too good to leave behind. From there, Sage builds a whole direction around the clothes.</p>
      <p>She does not curate around one fixed aesthetic. She follows the feeling of the pieces and mixes secondhand finds into collections that feel specific without feeling costume-like.</p>
      <p>The shop is meant to be approachable, too. You can ask questions, talk through a style idea, or admit that you have no idea what the right fashion word is.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section point-of-view-section">
    <span class="eyebrow">Not one aesthetic. One point of view.</span>
    <div class="mood-ribbon" aria-label="Good Intentions brand moods">
      {siteData.brand.confirmedWords.map((word) => <span>{word}</span>)}
      <span>music-inspired</span>
      <span>secondhand</span>
      <span>a little unexpected</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section about-belief-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Why secondhand</span>
      <h2>The interesting clothes already exist.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>Good Intentions is about keeping good pieces moving, making personal style feel less disposable, and giving clothes another chance to land with the person who will actually wear them.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section about-quote-section">
    <blockquote>Good clothes do not have to match one trend. They just have to feel right on the person wearing them.</blockquote>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
